<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79990" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάτᾰγος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[πᾰ]</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>clatter, crash</i>,
			as of trees falling, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δέ τε
			ἀγνυμενάων</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίγνεται</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.769
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δέ τε γίγνετ᾽ ὀδόντων</span>
			<i>chattering</i> of the teeth, <i><span class="en">
				13.283
			</span></i> ; <i>plash</i> of a body falling into water, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δ᾽ ἔπεσον μεγάλῳ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				21.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.24
			</span></i> ; <i>rattle</i> or <i>crash</i> of thunder, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				382
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				395a13
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀνέμων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>rumbling</i> caused by flatulence, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				22
			</span></i> ; but never of the human voice (exc. in late Greek, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βληχᾶσθαι καὶ κρώζειν ἐν ὑποκρίσει τὸν
				ἔξηχον π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				35
			</span></i>) : hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῇ καὶ
				πατά&lt;&gt; ῳ χρεώμενοι</span> means, with a
			great shouting and <i>clashing</i> of arms, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.79
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.211
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δορός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					103
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόξων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					518
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπίδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					832
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				539
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. χύτρειος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					329
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). (Onomatop. word.)</div>
